5. WIPED OPENAI CODEX ENGINEERING DOCS CITING CWSBP TYPESCRIPT SOURCE FILES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--- 9bbd8177af~1:docs/storm-behavior-port.md (wiped in 9bbd8177af 'ohmama' on 2026-09-11) ---
  L3: Decayed's existing TickBus, Scheduler, caches, growth scoreboards, native phase events and hunt controller remain the behavior owners. CWSBP's CommandedWitherHead.ts, WitherStormFlying.ts, ClusterAbsorbSystem.ts and WitherStormMod.ts were used as references. Rider order, nearest-owner searches, dimension-wide scans and the external phase numbering were not imported.
  L67: - Changed TypeScript and JSON contain no imported CWSBP namespaces. The regenerated bundle still includes two pre-existing keys, falling_block:layers and falling_block:custom_component, from Decayed's unchanged falling-block implementation; both were verified in the base commit.

--- b0ea0aaa42~1:src/clusters/STORM_FALLING_BLOCKS.md (wiped in b0ea0aaa42 'a quite config change!' on 2026-08-11) ---
  L3: ## CWSBP reference
  L5: Decayed's storm debris now follows the CWSBP `BP/entities/blocks/falling_block.json` + `BP/src/entities/BlockCluster.ts` model instead of emulating gravity with `decayed:cluster`.
  L7: CWSBP's `witherstormmod:falling_block`:
  L34: | Sustained Play Dead | CWS 30% tick chance, 5 blocks per successful emission while still above the CWS-style 8-block ground threshold |
  L39: | Actual death | immediate 20-block burst, then a detached 140-tick emitter using CWS's 40% emission chance and 40% big-block chance |
  L77: 3. for `mark_variant=5`, place 2-4 additional random registered withered/flesh blocks nearby, approximating CWSBP's large-debris flesh deposit

--- 26a95360ac~1:src/clusters/STORM_DEATH_SCATTER.md (wiped in 26a95360ac 'beca cultural' on 2026-08-09) ---
  L3: ## CWSBP reference
  L5: The `Main-Development` CWSBP implementation is split between `BP/src/entities/WitherStorm.ts` and `BP/src/entities/BlockCluster.ts`.
  L7: CWSBP separates debris emission from motion: Play Dead emits debris during the descent, death emits a denser shower, and each visible block receives an outward randomized launch. Decayed Reality keeps that visual language while reusing its own cluster renderer.
  L84: Death is deliberately more deterministic than the earlier CWS-style probability-only implementation so flesh debris is always visible during the sequence.

